# Works in Visual Studio 2022 (17.8+) and in VS Code (REST Client extension).
# Start the service first (docker compose up --build  OR  dotnet run --project src/ReviewService).

@host = http://localhost:5080

### Health (is the database reachable?)
GET {{host}}/health/ready

### 1) Create a review task without Kafka (Development only)
POST {{host}}/dev/review-requests
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "claimId": "CLM-1001",
  "policyId": "POL-77",
  "customerId": "CUS-5",
  "claimedAmount": 1200.00,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "riskScore": 0.45,
  "riskReasons": [ "Amount above the auto-approval limit of 300 EUR" ],
  "recommendation": "Approve",
  "summary": "Policy valid, receipt and photo attached. Amount exceeds the automatic limit."
}

### 2) The work queue (oldest first)
GET {{host}}/reviews?status=Pending

### 3) Open one review (replace the id with one from the list above)
GET {{host}}/reviews/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### 4) Take it
POST {{host}}/reviews/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/assign

### 5) Decide: Approved | Rejected | NeedsMoreInfo
POST {{host}}/reviews/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/decision
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "decision": "Approved",
  "reason": "Documents are complete and consistent."
}

### 6) Audit trail of a review
GET {{host}}/reviews/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/history

### Pretend to be another employee (Auth:Mode=Disabled only)
POST {{host}}/reviews/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/assign
X-Dev-User: ana
X-Dev-Roles: reviewer
